  "result": "Perfect! I've successfully implemented line discounts for the invoice system. Here's what was added:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n**Error handling (errors.js)**\n- Added `DISCOUNT_INVALID` error for invalid discount percentages\n\n**Invoice functions (invoices.js)**\n- Added `isValidDiscount()` helper to validate discounts are numbers between 0-100 (decimals allowed)\n- Updated `createInvoice()` to accept and validate `discountPercent` on lines, defaulting to 0\n- Added `lineDiscount()` function to calculate discount amount (line total \u00d7 discountPercent / 100), clamped at 0\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` to return `{ subtotal, discount, total }` with total = subtotal - discount (clamped at 0)\n- Updated `addLine()` to accept and validate `discountPercent`, keeping existing discount if not provided for existing lines\n\n**Tests (invoices.test.js)**\n- 27 new tests covering:\n  - Discount acceptance and defaults\n  - Validation (negative, over 100, non-numeric values)\n  - Decimal percentages (12.5%, etc.)\n  - Discount amount calculations\n  - Invoice totals with various discount scenarios\n  - Mixed discount/no-discount lines\n  - 100% discounts\n  - Proper clamping at 0\n\nAll 88 tests pass. The implementation ensures no computed amounts go below zero as specified.",
